# Deny-all, then explicitly allowlist what should actually deploy. A file
# being committed to git is NOT enough for it to go live -- it also has to
# be listed here, or Vercel silently drops it from the build and every
# route to it 404s even though vercel.json's rewrites/cleanUrls are fine.
# This bit twice: animus-audit-report.html and SOAK_TEST_AUDIT_REPORT.html
# were both committed and linked from live pages (index.html, benchmark.html
# link to the soak report; the audit report was requested directly) but
# 404'd on animusinfra.com until added here. 2026-09-16 audit: crawled every
# live page's internal href/src/action/fetch()/url() reference and curled
# each target -- all resolve 200 (or 405 for the POST-only /api endpoint)
# as of that check.
*
!index.html
!terms.html
!privacy.html
!benchmark.html
!whitepaper.html
!animus-audit-report.html
!SOAK_TEST_AUDIT_REPORT.html
!animus-one-pager.html
!vercel.json
!animus-logo.png
!animus-logo-mark.png
!animus-icon.png
!animus-icon-navbar.png
!api
!api/**

# Deliberately NOT allowlisted (2026-09-16 audit) -- none of these are
# linked from any live page, so leaving them out breaks nothing:
# - business-card.html: embeds a personal phone number + email in plain
#   HTML; kept off any public URL by choice, shared as a local file instead.
# - animus_client_deck.html, ANIMUS_CORE_AUDIT_WHITEPAPER.html,
#   social_snippet.html: unlinked collateral, no current need for a public
#   URL. Add an allowlist line here (and verify the route) if that changes.
